Rule 1 (split_size_or_sections should be non-negative and less than or equal to the size of the dimension if it's an integer; and dim should be within the range of the tensor's dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : int} |= v_2 ≥ 0 ∧ v_3 ≥ (0 - ndim(v_1)) ∧ v_3 < ndim(v_1) ∧ if ndim(v_1) > 0 then v_2 ≤ shape(v_1,v_3)
>>
Rule 2 (If split_size_or_sections is a list, then all the elements should be non-negative.)
{v_1 : list(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] ≥ 0
>>
Rule 3 (If split_size_or_sections is a list, the sum of the elements should be equal to the size of the dimension.)
{v_1 : list(int)} |= (∃i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] ≥ 0)
>>
Rule 4 (The dimension along which to split must be within the valid range for the tensor's dimensions.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= v_2 ≥ (0 - ndim(v_1)) ∧ v_2 < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 5 (If split_size_or_sections is an int and dimension size is 0, then split size can only be 0)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : int} |= if shape(v_1, v_3) = 0 then v_2 = 0
>>
Rule 6 (If split_size_or_sections is a list, then the list length should not be greater than the size of dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int), v_3 : int} |= v_2.len ≤ shape(v_1, v_3)
>>
Rule 7 (When split_size_or_sections is int, if dimension size can not be divided by split size then last chunk should be smaller)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : int} |= if (shape(v_1, v_3) / v_2) * v_2 ≠ shape(v_1, v_3) then true
>>
Rule 8 (split_size_or_sections cannot be greater than the total number of elements in the given dimension.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : int} |= v_2 ≤ shape(v_1, v_3)
